## LONG

**1. `lnhoyt-54mr` — rung 1, outage.** *Hoyt – Northland 115 kV*, 2026-08-14 23:34 → **2026-08-19 15:00**, covers all of 8/18. Match is by outage name against the `wr:hoytstra:345` contingency, not a topology link — the linked-outage query returned nothing for 793187/817362. Largest DA for 8/18 (−2383), largest RT yesterday (−3037), and **the only constraint binding in RT today hrs 1–8** (−205 RT / −102 DA). Binds all 24 hours, peak hr 18. Genuinely new: 7 RT days in the whole 104-week history, 4 of them this week, zero in Aug 2024 or 2025. *Wind or load:* neither separates cleanly — load lift only 3.5×, wind −1.0, and it's on the **zone-4 default** (no sheet mapping), so the lift was measured against OKGE forecasts for a Westar Kansas element. Low-confidence attribution; the call rests entirely on the outage plus the RT print.

**2. `lnrussett-sbrown` — rung 1 + 3, the biggest disagreement on the board.** Linked outage *Pittsburg 345 (PSO) – Valliant 345 kV*, **2026-08-17 07:30 → 2026-08-21 17:00** — started yesterday, live through the bid date. **RT-only: absent from tomorrow's DA entirely**, yet it bound RT yesterday at −1834 and on **29 of the last 30 days** (376 RT days in 104 weeks; 7 days in this same Aug window in 2024 and 2026). Binds overnight, hrs 20–08, peak hr 1. *Wind or load:* **wind**, zone 3 (real sheet mapping) — top-5% wind lifts binding 0.35 → 0.73; load lift is negative (−0.41). **The wind condition does not reproduce tomorrow**: zone-3 overnight wind sits at the 25–40th pct, not the top 5%. So this is an outage-and-frequency call, not a condition call — size it on the 29/30 hit rate and the live 345 outage, and expect a weaker print than the last few nights.

**3. `lnmdwst-frnkln1` — rung 1 + 2, highest-conviction PDF-backed call.** The 8/07 write-up names *PITTSB9 2160 A LN* (Pittsburg–Valliant 345) as the aggravating outage — LODF 1.8%, flow impact 4.2%, risk multiplier 1.61× — and explicitly notes it *"ended early in RT, which would have relieved the constraint."* **That outage is back**, 8/17 07:30 → 8/21 17:00, so 8/18 has the trigger the write-up describes, restored. *Canadian River 345/138 kV Transformer* is also out through 8/31, and the contingency is `okgewfec:cdrlncanadn1noble4wal`. Driver per PDF: *"high load in the WFEC zone (aggravating) combined with a massive loss of relief from the OKGE zone"*, Peak Load 4.4×. Tomorrow reproduces the load side — zone 4 at the 100th pct in hrs 18–19, which is precisely when it binds (hr 18–21, peak hr 20). 17 of 30 RT days, all 17 of its all-time RT days are in the last month. *Wind or load:* **load**, 13.8× lift, zone-4 default (WFEC/OKGE element, so zone 4 is at least the right neighbourhood).

**4. `ln6_me4-sw51` — rung 1 + 2.** Linked outage *Mustang OKGE – SW 5th 138 kV*, 2026-08-03 08:00 → **2026-08-27 14:00**, well past the bid date. DA −1114 for 8/18; RT 13 of 30 days (13 of 13 all-time — activated with the outage). Binds hrs 14–20, peak hr 16. *Wind or load:* **load**, zone 4, **16.3× lift — the highest in the candidate set**; wind lift −1.0. Zone 4 load hits the 90–100th pct exactly across hrs 16–19. Zone mapping is the default, but the element is OKGE so the zone-4 forecast is appropriate. Condition and outage both point the same way.

**5. `lnseminole-maud_tap` — rung 3, new and frequent.** 19 of 30 RT days (31 all-time — again, newly active). RT yesterday −667 against DA −646, i.e. DA priced it correctly; DA −1331 for 8/18. Binds hrs 12–19, peak hr 18. *Wind or load:* **load**, 14.6× lift, zone-4 default — OKGE element, zone appropriate. Zone 4 evening load at the 100th pct is the tailwind. No outage on its path and no PDF section, so this rests on frequency plus condition match alone.

**6. `lnlubbocks-lubbocke` — rung 1, small size, zone conflict.** New outage *South Plains REC Abernathy Sub – Tuco Interchange 69 kV*, **2026-08-18 08:00 → 08-19 16:00**, plus *Hale Center Sub – Tuco Interchange 69 kV* running through 11/06 — both Lubbock-area. 9 of 30 RT days (10 all-time); RT yesterday −800 against DA only −364, so RT beat DA; DA −648 for 8/18. Binds hrs 11–20. **Zone conflict, flag it:** the sheet has no mapping, so the lift was run against zone 4 (15.0× load). This is an SPS Lubbock element and plausibly zone 5 — where tomorrow's setup is on-peak load at the 22nd pct and wind at the **3rd**, the opposite of the peak-load condition the lift wants. Rung 1 outranks rung 5, so I keep it long, but small, and the attribution is low-confidence.

