## SHORT

**1. `xfmrnowst1-nowst1` — rung 5, cleanest short on the board.** Largest DA yesterday (−3458) and −851 DA for 8/18, and it has **never bound in RT — zero RT days in the entire 104-week history**. The 8/13 PDF describes exactly this failure mode: *"DA bound at −1989, RT cleared at 0… caused by a 5,626 MW over-forecast of wind at the binding hour (HE 17). Since wind in OKGE is a loading driver, the DA model placed significantly more flow on the constraint than materialized in RT."* It is the only candidate with a **positive wind lift** (2.95×) alongside load (10.8×), consistent with wind being a loading driver. No outages in its topology model. Tomorrow's zone-4 on-peak wind at the 58th pct gives the DA model the same room to over-forecast.

**2. `lnnebrcty-sub3456` — rung 5, expired trigger.** Zone 1 is a **real sheet mapping**, and the lift is unambiguous: **load** 2.58×, wind −0.93 — a peak-load constraint that binds hrs 15–19. **Tomorrow's zone-1 load contradicts that**: on-peak median 41st pct, and hrs 17–21 fall to 29/23/16/26/10. The PDF (8/10) says it is *"structurally predisposed to bind during peak load conditions"* and that the acute trigger was the **forced** *JASPER7 JASPER_MORGAN A LN* outage, 8/10 08:00, **no end time**, risk multiplier **11.47×**. That forced outage does not appear in the 8/18 scheduled list. What remains is *Cooper–Fairport 345* (1.29×, through 8/21) and *Split Rock–White* (1.00×) — the weak ones. DA has it at −588 for 8/18; RT yesterday was −8. Acute trigger gone, load condition inverted: short.

**3. `lnftrandl-spence1` — rung 5.** DA-only, −572 for 8/18, **zero RT days in the last 30**. The 8/07 PDF attributes its −9500 RT print to *"a significant under-forecast of NPPD zonal load… actual NPPD load came in an average of 561 MW higher than the DA forecast"*, Peak Load 4.7×, *"no transmission outages were present."* NPPD is zone 1, where tomorrow's load is 41st-pct on-peak and collapsing after hr 16 — the peak-load condition does not reproduce. **Zone disagreement:** the sheet has no mapping so the lift ran on zone 4 (7.5× load); prefer the PDF's NPPD/zone-1 read, which is the bearish one. Note there are Spencer-area 69 kV outages on 8/18 (*Spencer Center – Spencer E. Jct.*, 8/17 13:00 → 8/19 10:00, plus two longer ones) — but those are Iowa Spencer, not Spencer NE, so I am not treating them as a rung-1 trigger.

**4. `lnsiouxfl-moodyco` — rung 5.** Third-largest DA for 8/18 (−1263) and **zero RT in 104 weeks**; 5 DA days in this Aug window in 2026, none in 2024 or 2025. WAUE eastern-South-Dakota element (`waue:brookngsaurorawa:115`). *Split Rock – White 345 kV Ckt 1* is out through 8/20 and *Granite Falls 230/115 XFMR #2* through 8/20, both nearby — which is likely why DA keeps pricing it — but two full weeks of DA prints have produced no RT whatsoever. **Zone-4 default is the wrong forecast** for a WAUE element, so the 10.0× load lift is not usable. Short on the DA-only record.

**5. `lnhuron-woonskt` — rung 5.** DA-only, −900 for 8/18, **zero RT ever**, and only **one** DA day in this calendar window across the full 104 weeks. WAUE South Dakota (`waue:ftthompwessprng:230`), no outage on its path in the 8/18 list, not in the PDF. Zone-4 default is again the wrong zone (the 19.0× lift comes off a 0.0002 baseline — 2 events; ignore it). Nothing supports it except tomorrow's DA.

**6. `lnbrook_ln-junctn5` — rung 5.** In yesterday's DA at −787, **absent from tomorrow's DA**, zero RT ever, 4 DA days this Aug window and none in prior years. Springfield MO 161 kV (`sprm:main1batfld5:161`). Zone-4 default, wrong zone. No reason to carry it.

**7. `lncommtap4-bois_tap` — rung 5.** In yesterday's DA at −991, **absent from tomorrow's DA**, zero RT ever despite 8 DA days in this window. `csws:santafe4cornvill:138`. Zone-4 default. Same call.

