## Gaps

- **PDF window 8/07–8/13 ends four days before the bid date.** Three of fourteen candidates have a write-up. `ln6_me4-sw51`, `lnbrook_ln-junctn5`, `lncommtap4-bois_tap`, `lnhoyt-54mr`, `lnhuron-woonskt`, `lnlubbocks-lubbocke`, `lnrussett-sbrown`, `lnseminole-maud_tap`, `lnsiouxfl-moodyco`, `xfmrvalliant-valliant` are **absent from the PDF** — including two of my top three longs.
- `xfmrnowst1-nowst1` is in the PDF only as **`xfmrnowst1-nowst1_rev23`**; the exact-name header index missed it and I had to fetch it separately. Any future run indexing by exact name will silently drop it.
- **11 of 14 candidates have no `reserve_zone` in the sheet** and fell back to zone 4. Only `lnnebrcty-sub3456` (1), `lnrussett-sbrown` (3) and `xfmrnowst1-nowst1` (4) are real mappings. Every zone-4-default lift above is measured against OKGE forecasts; for the WAUE (`lnsiouxfl-moodyco`, `lnhuron-woonskt`), SPS (`lnlubbocks-lubbocke`), NPPD (`lnftrandl-spence1`), WR (`lnhoyt-54mr`) and SPRM (`lnbrook_ln-junctn5`) elements that is the wrong zone.
- **Zone 21 load percentile is 0.0 at all 24 hours.** The forecast sits below the entire trailing month at every hour — that is a data problem, not a signal. Zone 21 load is unusable for tomorrow.
- **No uplift raised** — all 14 `analyze_constraint_by_zone` calls completed.
- Two lifts are built on near-empty baselines and should not be leaned on: `lnhuron-woonskt` (baseline 0.0002, ~2 events) and `lnbrook_ln-junctn5` (0.0026).
- **Regime note:** `ln6_me4-sw51`, `lnmdwst-frnkln1`, `lnlubbocks-lubbocke`, `lnhoyt-54mr` and `lnseminole-maud_tap` have essentially their entire RT history inside the last 30 days. Five OKGE/SPS constraints activating at once is a network change, not five independent events — the 104-week history offers no seasonal precedent for any of them, so the momentum calls are thinner than the day counts suggest.
